# EtFabMenu Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtFabMenu` is a Floating Action Button (FAB) menu for the eToro design system. It expands from a primary trigger to reveal multiple related actions in a vertical stack above the trigger.

- **Compound component pattern**: `EtFabMenu.Trigger`, `EtFabMenu.Actions`, `EtFabMenu.Button`
- **Default trigger**: Circular FAB with star/close icon based on state
- **Custom trigger**: Accepts `EtButton` or render-prop function for custom content
- **Close on outside press**: Transparent overlay closes menu when tapping outside (configurable)
- **Close on action**: Menu automatically closes when an action is selected

**Does NOT handle:**

- Positioning (consumer places the component, e.g. `position: absolute`, bottom-right)
- Navigation logic (use with router handlers in `onPress`)
- More than 5 actions (design guideline: 3–5 max recommended)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtFabMenu` (root)

```tsx
<EtFabMenu
  closeOnOutsidePress?: boolean   // default: true
  contentInset?: { bottom?: number; right?: number }   // when menu opens in Modal; match parent position
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
>
  {children}
</EtFabMenu>
```

**Children:** Must include `EtFabMenu.Trigger` and `EtFabMenu.Actions`.

**contentInset:** When `closeOnOutsidePress` is true and the menu opens, content renders in a Modal. Pass `contentInset` with the same `bottom`/`right` values as your positioning container so the FAB stays fixed (no jump).

### `EtFabMenu.Trigger`

```tsx
<EtFabMenu.Trigger>
  {children?: ReactNode | ((isOpen: boolean) => ReactNode)}
</EtFabMenu.Trigger>
```

- **No children**: Renders default circular FAB (44×44, primary green, star/close icon)
- **Children (EtButton)**: Clones and adds `onPress` to toggle
- **Children (function)**: Receives `isOpen`, e.g. `(isOpen) => <EtButton><EtButton.Icon name={isOpen ? 'close' : 'plus'} /></EtButton>`

### `EtFabMenu.Actions`

```tsx
<EtFabMenu.Actions>
  {EtFabMenu.Button[]}
</EtFabMenu.Actions>
```

Only `EtFabMenu.Button` children are valid. Invalid children are filtered out with a `__DEV__` warning.

### `EtFabMenu.Button`

```tsx
<EtFabMenu.Button
  iconName: IconName    // required
  label: string         // required
  onPress: () => void   // required
  disabled?: boolean    // default: false
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string  // defaults to label
/>
```

## Usage

### Basic (default trigger)

```tsx
<EtFabMenu>
  <EtFabMenu.Trigger />
  <EtFabMenu.Actions>
    <EtFabMenu.Button iconName="star" label="Action 01" onPress={handle1} />
    <EtFabMenu.Button iconName="heart" label="Action 02" onPress={handle2} />
  </EtFabMenu.Actions>
</EtFabMenu>
```

### With custom trigger (EtButton)

```tsx
<EtFabMenu>
  <EtFabMenu.Trigger>
    <EtButton>
      <EtButton.Icon name="plus" />
    </EtButton>
  </EtFabMenu.Trigger>
  <EtFabMenu.Actions>...</EtFabMenu.Actions>
</EtFabMenu>
```

### With icon swap (render prop)

```tsx
<EtFabMenu>
  <EtFabMenu.Trigger>
    {(isOpen) => (
      <EtButton>
        <EtButton.Icon name={isOpen ? 'close' : 'plus'} />
      </EtButton>
    )}
  </EtFabMenu.Trigger>
  <EtFabMenu.Actions>...</EtFabMenu.Actions>
</EtFabMenu>
```

### Positioned (e.g. bottom-right)

```tsx
<View style={{ flex: 1 }}>
  <Content />
  <View style={{ position: 'absolute', bottom: 100, right: 16 }}>
    <EtFabMenu contentInset={{ bottom: 100, right: 16 }}>
      <EtFabMenu.Trigger />
      <EtFabMenu.Actions>...</EtFabMenu.Actions>
    </EtFabMenu>
  </View>
</View>
```

Pass `contentInset` with the same values as your container's `bottom`/`right` so the FAB position stays fixed when the menu opens.

## Design System Integration

- **Colors** (from `useEtoroTheme().colors`):
  - Trigger: `bgActionBrand`
  - Action items: `bgPositiveForthiary`
  - Text/icon: `textPrimaryNeutral`, `textInvertedPrimaryNeutral`
- **Sizes & spacing**:
  - FAB: 44×44, padding X2, borderRadius FAB_SIZE/2 (circular)
  - Action items: height 44, icon 20×20, padding X3 (vertical) X4 (horizontal), borderRadius ACTION_HEIGHT/2 (pill), icon-text gap X2
  - Trigger icon: 20×20

## States & Behavior

- **Default**: Collapsed
- **On trigger press**: Expands to reveal actions
- **Main FAB icon**: Star when closed, Close when open (default trigger)
- **Action press**: Executes callback, closes menu
- **Outside press**: Closes menu (when `closeOnOutsidePress={true}`)
- **Android back**: `onRequestClose` on Modal closes menu (native-only via `core/web/modal-request-close` — RNW's Modal would otherwise ALSO close on Escape keyup, behind the dismiss stack's back)
- **ESC key (web)**: Closes menu via the shared dismiss stack (`core/web/use-dismissable`, topmost open layer only)

## Usage Guidelines (from design system)

**Do:**
- Keep actions limited (3–5 max recommended)
- Ensure all actions are closely related
- Use clear iconography
- Close menu after selection (handled automatically)

**Avoid:**
- Using as a replacement for navigation menus
- Including unrelated actions
- Overloading with too many options

## Anti-patterns

❌ **Non-Button children in Actions** – Only `EtFabMenu.Button` allowed

❌ **Using as navigation** – FAB menu is for contextual actions, not primary navigation

❌ **Too many actions** – Keep 3–5 max per design guidelines

## Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` – theme colors
- `EtButton`, `EtoroIcon`, `EtText` – primitives
- `expo-haptics` – haptic feedback
- `Modal`, `Pressable` – React Native
